 de Crau","dish/foin-de-crau"],["Fraisier","dish/fraisier"],["French onion soup","dish/french-onion-soup"],["French restaurant","dish/french-restaurant"],["Fricassee","dish/fricassee"],["Garbure","dish/garbure"],["Gâteau Basque","dish/gateau-basque"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/05/C%C3%B4te_de_boeuf_ma%C3%AEtre_d%27h%C3%B4tel.jpg/500px-C%C3%B4te_de_boeuf_ma%C3%AEtre_d%27h%C3%B4tel.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Arnaud 25","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:C%C3%B4te_de_boeuf_ma%C3%AEtre_d'h%C3%B4tel.jpg"}},"ingredient/waffle":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/waffle","n":"Waffle","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["A waffle is a dish made from usually leavened batter or dough that is cooked between two plates that are patterned to give a characteristic size, shape, and surface impression. There are many variations based on the type of waffle iron and recipe used. Waffles are eaten throughout the world, particularly in Belgium, which has over a dozen regional varieties.  Waffles may be made fresh or simply heated after having been commercially baked and packaged fresh or frozen."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-waffle"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waffle"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Algerian cuisine","cuisine/algerian-cuisine",[["Zviti","dish/zviti"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Croffle","dish/croffle"]]],["Irish cuisine","cuisine/irish-cuisine",[["Croffle","dish/croffle"]]],["South Korean cuisine","cuisine/south-korean-cuisine",[["Croffle","dish/croffle"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Croissant","ingredient/croissant"],["Rakhsas","ingredient/rakhsas"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/5b/Waffles_with_Strawberries.jpg/500px-Waffles_with_Strawberries.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Parkerman & Christie from San Diego, USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waffles_with_Strawberries.jpg"}},"ingredient/goat":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/goat","n":"Goat","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 9 dishes across 7 cuisines","intro":[["Goat meat is the meat of the domestic goat (Capra hircus). The term denotes especially the meat of older animals, while meat from young goats is called kid meat. In South Asian cuisine, goat meat is commonly called \"mutton\", which elsewhere in the world means sheep meat."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-goat"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goat_meat"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":7,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Mie aceh","dish/mie-aceh"],["Nasi kebuli","dish/nasi-kebuli"],["Satay","dish/satay"],["Sate kambing","dish/sate-kambing"],["Sate klatak","dish/sate-klatak"],["Tongseng","dish/tongseng"]]],["Acehnese cuisine","cuisine/acehnese-cuisine",[["Mie aceh","dish/mie-aceh"]]],["Georgian cuisine","cuisine/georgian-cuisine",[["Kubdari","dish/kubdari"]]],["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine",[["Hyderabadi haleem","dish/hyderabadi-haleem"]]],["Nigerian cuisine","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine",[["Suya","dish/suya"]]],["Singaporean Chinese cuisine","cuisine/singaporean-cuisine-chinese-inspired",[["Satay","dish/satay"]]],["Singaporean cuisine","cuisine/singaporean-cuisine",[["Satay","dish/satay"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Meat of goat, fresh or chilled","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":7324792,"top":[["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",2528329],["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",1440788],["Pakistan","cuisine/pakistani-cuisine",532222],["Nigeria","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine",2