mmon bread, but is often served with added vegetables such as celery, parsley, mint, basil leaves, or garden cress. It may also be prepared with meat, cheese, vegetables, and onion."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-khubz-al-abbas"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khubz_al-%CA%BEAbbas"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Iraqi cuisine","cuisine/iraqi-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Iraqi Family Cookbook","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"iraqifamilycookbook.blogspot.com","note":"Long-running blog of Iraqi family recipes tied to the cookbook of the same name.","url":"https://iraqifamilycookbook.blogspot.com/2014","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Iraqi cuisine","links":[["Qeema Najafi","dish/qeema-najafi"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/50/Abbas_bread_01.jpg/500px-Abbas_bread_01.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Ayat Jaryan","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abbas_bread_01.jpg"}},"ingredient/boston-butt":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/boston-butt","n":"Boston butt","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A Boston butt is a slightly wedge-shaped portion cut of the pork shoulder located above the standard picnic cut. It includes the blade bone or may be sold as a boneless “lean butt,” and it can be used as a substitutes for tenderloin in certain preparations. The pork shoulder is generally classified as a primal cut, with the picnic and butt portions considered sub-primal cuts. Some sources, however, refer to the butt itself as a primary cut."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-boston-butt"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston_butt"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked w